#v(0.4em)

Hi,

I'm applying for the Applied AI Engineer role because it sits right where I already
spend my time: building with AI agents, and caring about the interface and the system
underneath in equal measure. "Agentic systems and user-facing applications deployed in
real customer environments" reads like a description of what I do for fun.

Concretely, I work in an agent-driven setup every day (Claude Code, MCP, local models
on my home lab) and have built my own small agent harnesses, so multi-agent workflows
with tool use and evaluation loops are familiar ground rather than a phrase on a
job ad. On the fullstack side I'm comfortable across TypeScript and React, from GraphQL
and REST APIs down to the data model, which lines up with building the interactive UIs
and cross-stack integrations the role describes.

Reasoning over real-world data is something I've done too. In my bachelor project with
Aker Solutions I planned the architecture for a dashboard that turns time-series sensor
data into something an operator can actually read and act on. From earlier user-support
work I'm also used to translating technical detail for non-technical people, which is
the "evangelize and enable" part of the role.

I won't pretend to have years behind me; I'm finishing my informatics degree. But the
specific overlap here, agents, fullstack, and making data legible, is unusually close
to how I already work, and I'd be glad to talk.

#v(0.6em)
Best regards, \
*Philip Bjørknes Krogh*
